from ch17_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(167, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD CHOSE HIM OF ALL YOUR TRIBES" (18:5) — TEACHES THAT SERVICE IS VALID ONLY STANDING; IF HE SAT AND MINISTERED, HIS SERVICE IS INVALID. The head row of piska 167 ({SP_(167, 1, "מגיד", "שאין", "שרות", "כשר", "בו", "אלא", "מעומד")} "teaches that service is valid in him only standing"): "TO STAND AND MINISTER" (one seat, asserted) — 155:5\'s rule at its own verse: the compile\'s service posture. Fresh.')
srow(167, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE AND HIS SONS ALL THE DAYS" — IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE IT. ({SP_(167, 2, "בין", "בארץ", "ובין", "בחוצה", "לארץ")} "whether in the land or outside the land"): the priesthood\'s choice everywhere (Tosefta Taanit 4:1) — "all the days" as all places: the compile\'s priesthood status unconditioned on the land. Fresh.')
srow(168, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHEN THE LEVITE COMES" (18:6) — MIGHT THE VERSE SPEAK OF A LEVITE PROPER? "FROM ONE OF YOUR GATES" — THOSE WHO DID NOT TAKE THEIR GATES ELSEWHERE; THE LEVITES, WHO TOOK THEIR GATES ELSEWHERE, ARE OUT. "AND HE SHALL MINISTER" (18:7) — ONE FIT TO MINISTER; THE LEVITES, UNFIT TO MINISTER, ARE OUT. The head row of piska 168 ({SP_(168, 1, "יכול", "בבן", "לוי", "ודי", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "might the verse speak of a Levite proper"; {SP_(168, 1, "יצאו", "לוים", "שאין", "ראויים", "לשרת")} "the Levites are out, who are unfit to minister"): "THE LEVITE" HERE IS A PRIEST — the book\'s "priests the Levites" (the English\'s note) read into the singular: the Levites of the cities (Numbers 35 the kin) excluded twice: the compile\'s subject the priest of the watches, not the tribe. Fresh.')
srow(168, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM ALL ISRAEL WHERE HE SOJOURNS" — IN ALL THE PLACES OF THEIR DWELLINGS. ({SP_(168, 2, "בכל", "מקומות", "מושבותיהם")} "in all the places of their dwellings"): the priest from anywhere in the land — the Levite "sojourns" (the participle, asserted): the compile\'s origin unconstrained. Fresh.')
srow(168, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND COMES WITH ALL THE DESIRE OF HIS SOUL" — WHENCE THAT A PRIEST COMES AND LIFTS HIS HANDS AT A WATCH NOT HIS OWN? "AND COMES WITH ALL THE DESIRE OF HIS SOUL". ({SP_(168, 3, "כהן", "בא", "ונושא", "את", "כפיו", "במשמר", "שאינו", "שלו")} "a priest comes and lifts his hands at a watch not his own"): THE PRIESTLY BLESSING OUT OF TURN — "with all the desire of his soul" (one seat, asserted; chapter 12\'s "your soul" thrice): the watch (the fifty-two shifts, the English\'s note) a schedule the desire may cross for the blessing: the compile\'s watches parameter with an exception. Fresh.')
srow(168, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ALL THE WATCHES ARE EQUAL IN THE FESTIVAL\'S OFFERINGS THAT COME BECAUSE OF THE FESTIVAL? "AND COMES WITH ALL THE DESIRE OF HIS SOUL". ALWAYS? "FROM ONE OF YOUR GATES" — WHEN ISRAEL IS GATHERED IN ONE GATE, AT THE THREE FEASTS. ({SP_(168, 4, "כל", "המשמרות", "שוים", "בקרבנות", "הרגל")} "all the watches are equal in the festival\'s offerings"; {SP_(168, 4, "בשלש", "רגלים")} "at the three feasts"): THE FESTIVAL\'S OFFERINGS SHARED BY ALL THE WATCHES, and only then — "one of your gates" read as ONE GATE for all Israel: the pilgrimage (16:16\'s cell) the condition; the parser\'s silence at "from one" (asserted) the instrument\'s fact beside the shelf\'s reading: the compile\'s watches suspended at the three feasts. Fresh.')
srow(169, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL MINISTER IN THE NAME OF THE LORD HIS GOD" (18:7) — ON THE FLOOR. FROM HERE YOU SAY (MISHNAH ZEVACHIM 2:1): THE UNCIRCUMCISED, THE UNCLEAN, THE SEATED, ONE STANDING ON VESSELS OR ON A BEAST OR ON HIS FELLOW\'S FEET — INVALID. The head row of piska 169 ({SP_(169, 1, "על", "גבי", "הרצפה")} "on the floor"; {SP_(169, 1, "או", "על", "גבי", "רגלי", "חברו", "פסול")} "or on his fellow\'s feet — invalid"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — the service\'s posture completed: barefoot on the stone, five disqualifications (155:5 and 167:1 the standing): the compile\'s service validity a five-condition check. Fresh.')
srow(169, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE (MISHNAH SUKKAH 5:7) THAT ALL THE WATCHES ARE EQUAL IN THE FESTIVAL\'S LIMBS AND IN THE DIVISION OF THE SHOWBREAD? "PORTION AS PORTION THEY SHALL EAT" (18:8) — A PORTION TO EAT, A PORTION TO SERVE; THE PORTION OF EATING AS THE PORTION OF SERVICE. ({SP_(169, 2, "באימורי", "רגלים", "ובחלוק", "לחם", "הפנים")} "in the festival\'s limbs and in the division of the showbread"; {SP_(169, 2, "חלק", "לאכול", "חלק", "לעבוד")} "a portion to eat, a portion to serve"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW A SECOND TIME — 18:8\'s doubled "portion" (one seat, asserted; the verse without a kin) read as EATING EQUAL TO SERVICE: the compile\'s festival distribution a rule of equality across the watches. Fresh.')
srow(169, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT ALL THE WATCHES BE EQUAL IN THE FESTIVAL\'S OFFERINGS THAT DO NOT COME BECAUSE OF THE FESTIVAL? "BESIDES HIS SALES ACCORDING TO THE FATHERS" — WHAT DID THE FATHERS SELL EACH OTHER? "YOU YOUR SABBATH AND I MY SABBATH". ({SP_(169, 3, "לבד", "ממכריו", "על", "האבות")} "besides his sales according to the fathers"; {SP_(169, 3, "אתה", "שבתך", "ואני", "שבתי")} "you your sabbath and I my sabbath"): THE FATHERS\' BARTER — the watches\' weeks traded, the private offerings kept to the week\'s watch: AND ONKELOS WRITES THE SAME ("the watch that comes on the Sabbath, as the fathers ordained" — the verse rewritten as the row, asserted, one seat): the compile\'s watches a rota the fathers may swap — a parameter with a provenance. Fresh.')
srow(170, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU COME INTO THE LAND" (18:9) — DO THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE MATTER, FOR BY ITS REWARD YOU ENTER THE LAND. The head row of piska 170 ({SP_(170, 1, "עשה", "מצוה", "האמורה", "בענין")} "do the commandment said in the matter"): the entry formula a third time (156:1, here, 174:1) — the diviners\' bar among the entry\'s conditions. Fresh.')
srow(170, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU" — BY YOUR MERIT. ({SP_(170, 2, "בזכותך")} "by your merit"): 156:2 again. Fresh.')
srow(170, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT LEARN TO DO THE ABOMINATIONS OF THOSE NATIONS" — MIGHT YOU NOT BE PERMITTED TO LEARN IN ORDER TO TEACH AND UNDERSTAND? "TO DO" — TO DO YOU MAY NOT LEARN, BUT YOU MAY LEARN TO TEACH AND UNDERSTAND. ({SP_(170, 3, "לעשות", "אי", "אתה", "למד")} "to do you do not learn"; {SP_(170, 3, "אבל", "אתה", "למד", "להורות", "ולהבין")} "but you learn to teach and to understand"): THE BAR ON THE DEED, NOT THE KNOWLEDGE — the infinitive "to do" the hinge ("the abominations of the nations" here and Manasseh\'s, asserted): the compile\'s diviners cells may DESCRIBE the rites they bar — the code/data law\'s own warrant (Sanhedrin 68a the segment if a cell needs it). Fresh.')
srow(171, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THERE SHALL NOT BE FOUND AMONG YOU" (18:10) — TO WARN THE COURT ABOUT IT. The head row of piska 171 ({SP_(171, 1, "להזהיר", "בית", "דין", "על", "כך")} "to warn the court about it"): "FOUND" the court\'s duty (Sifra Acharei 13:22) — the passive verb read as the court\'s vigilance, as 148:1 read it as witnesses: the courts daemon the diviners\' bar\'s enforcer. Fresh.')
srow(171, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO PASSES HIS SON OR HIS DAUGHTER THROUGH THE FIRE" — ONLY HIS SON AND DAUGHTER; HIS SON\'S SON AND HIS DAUGHTER\'S SON — WHENCE? LEVITICUS 20:4 "WHEN HE GIVES OF HIS SEED TO MOLECH". ({SP_(171, 2, "בן", "בנו", "ובן", "בתו", "מנין")} "his son\'s son and his daughter\'s son — whence"): the grandchildren by "of his seed" (Sifra Kedoshim 10:6) — Leviticus 20\'s Molech (the kin\'s ledger lev_20) the widening verse. Fresh.')
srow(171, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'STILL I SAY: HERE FIRE, THERE MOLECH; WHENCE TO GIVE WHAT IS SAID HERE TO THERE AND THERE TO HERE? "PASSING" "PASSING" AN ANALOGY: AS HERE FIRE, SO THERE FIRE; AS THERE MOLECH, SO HERE MOLECH. YOU FIND: NOT UNTIL HE HANDS OVER AND PASSES THROUGH FIRE AND TO MOLECH — UNTIL THE TWO VERSES SAY IT; OTHERWISE WE HAVE NOT HEARD. ({SP_(171, 3, "נאמר", "העברה", "העברה", "לגזרה", "שוה")} "said passing, passing — an analogy by the shared word"; {SP_(171, 3, "עד", "שימסור", "ויעביר", "באש", "ובמולך")} "until he hands over and passes through fire and to Molech"): THE TWO VERSES ONE LAW — fire from here, Molech from there (Sanhedrin 7:7, Tosefta 10:4): the compile\'s fire-passing effect requires BOTH conditions; 18:10 shares nothing in order with Leviticus 20:2 (asserted) — the analogy carries what the words do not. Fresh.')
srow(171, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"A DIVINER OF DIVINATIONS" — ONE WHO DIVINES MUCH AND ONE WHO DIVINES LITTLE ALIKE, LIABLE FOR EACH DIVINATION. ({SP_(171, 4, "לחיב", "על", "כל", "קסם", "וקסם")} "to make liable for each and every divination"): the doubled noun read as EVERY ACT LIABLE — the diviner\'s word at Balaam\'s "no divination in Israel" (Numbers 23:23, asserted): the compile\'s augury effect per act. Fresh.')
srow(171, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'WHAT IS A DIVINER? ONE WHO HOLDS HIS STAFF AND SAYS "SHALL I GO OR NOT GO?", AND SO HOSEA 4:12 "MY PEOPLE ASKS ITS WOOD AND ITS STAFF TELLS IT". ANOTHER WORD: A FOX ON HIS RIGHT OR HIS LEFT. ({SP_(171, 5, "זה", "האוחז", "במקלו", "ואומר")} "this is one who holds his staff and says"; {SP_(171, 5, "שועל", "בימינו", "ומשמאלו")} "a fox on his right and on his left"): THE DIVINER DEFINED — the staff oracle (Tosefta Shabbat 7:4\'s "Amorite ways") and the fox: the compile\'s augury a described rite, learned to understand (170:3). Fresh.')
srow(171, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHO PASSES HIS SON OR DAUGHTER THROUGH THE FIRE" — THIS IS ONE WHO LIES WITH AN ARAMEAN WOMAN AND RAISES FROM HER A SON HOSTILE TO THE PLACE; THE PUNISHMENT WE HEARD, THE WARNING WE HAVE NOT — "THERE SHALL NOT BE FOUND AMONG YOU ONE WHO PASSES". R. JUDAH: ONE WHO PASSES HIS SON OR DAUGHTER TO IDOLATRY AND CUTS A COVENANT WITH IT, AS IT IS SAID "THE CALF WHICH THEY CUT IN TWO AND PASSED BETWEEN ITS PARTS" (JEREMIAH 34:18). ({SP_(171, 6, "זה", "הבועל", "ארמית")} "this is one who lies with an Aramean woman"; {SP_(171, 6, "ענש", "שמענו", "אזהרה", "לא", "שמענו")} "the punishment we heard, the warning we have not heard"; {SP_(171, 6, "העגל", "אשר", "כרתו", "לשנים")} "the calf which they cut in two"): the second reading of the fire — the son of the foreign union, and R. JUDAH\'S COVENANT CUT BETWEEN THE PARTS (Jeremiah\'s echo of Genesis 15:9-19 — the tape\'s own covenant line; the row read at Genesis 31\'s sitting for the pieces): the punishment-without-warning rule (the compile\'s effect needs a warning verse — this one). REREAD WHOLE (Genesis 31\'s sitting, gen_31_covenant_pieces).')
srow(171, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"A SOOTHSAYER" — R. ISHMAEL: THIS IS ONE WHO PASSES OVER THE EYE. ({SP_(171, 7, "זה", "המעביר", "על", "העין")} "this is one who passes over the eye"): the second agent noun defined by the eye (the root heard as "eye"; Sifra Kedoshim 6:2) — the first of three definitions. Fresh.')
srow(171, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: THESE ARE THE GIVERS OF TIMES — WHO SAY "THE EVE OF THE SEVENTH YEARS IS FIT FOR WHEAT, UPROOTED PULSE WILL BE BAD"; THE SAGES: THESE ARE THE HOLDERS OF THE EYES. ({SP_(171, 8, "אלו", "נותני", "העתים")} "these are the givers of times"; {SP_(171, 8, "אלו", "אוחזי", "העינים")} "these are the holders of the eyes"): the second and third definitions — the calendar-reader (the root heard as "season") and the illusionist (Tosefta Shabbat 7:14): the compile\'s soothsayer cell three-armed by the word\'s two roots (the row without a citation). Fresh.')
srow(171, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND AN OMEN-READER" — WHO IS AN OMEN-READER? ONE WHO SAYS "MY BREAD FELL FROM MY MOUTH, MY STAFF FROM MY HAND, A SNAKE PASSED ON MY RIGHT, A FOX ON MY LEFT, A DEER CUT THE ROAD BEFORE ME". ({SP_(171, 9, "נפלה", "פתי", "מפי")} "my bread fell from my mouth"; {SP_(171, 9, "עבר", "נחש", "מימיני")} "a snake passed on my right"): THE OMEN-READER DEFINED BY HIS OMENS (the snake his own root\'s word — Leviticus 19:26\'s pair, asserted): five omens the compile describes and bars. Fresh.')
srow(171, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"DO NOT BEGIN WITH ME — IT IS MORNING, IT IS THE NEW MOON, IT IS THE SABBATH\'S END". ({SP_(171, 10, "אל", "תתחיל", "בי")} "do not begin with me"; {SP_(171, 10, "מוצאי", "שבת", "הוא")} "it is the Sabbath\'s end"): three more omens of the calendar (Tosefta Shabbat 7:13; the row without a citation) — the reader\'s times. Fresh.')
srow(171, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND A SORCERER" — ONE WHO DOES A DEED, NOT ONE WHO HOLDS THE EYES. R. AKIVA IN R. JOSHUA\'S NAME: TWO GATHER CUCUMBERS — ONE GATHERS AND IS EXEMPT, ONE GATHERS AND IS LIABLE; THE DOER OF A DEED IS LIABLE, THE HOLDER OF THE EYES EXEMPT. ({SP_(171, 11, "העושה", "מעשה", "ולא", "האוחז", "את", "העינים")} "one who does a deed and not one who holds the eyes"; {SP_(171, 11, "שנים", "מלקטים", "קשואים")} "two gather cucumbers"): THE SORCERER A DOER — the cucumber case (Sanhedrin 7:11, the "from here" without a name; the sorceress of Exodus 22:17 the kin): the compile\'s sorcery liable on the deed alone, the illusion exempt — the same deed/appearance split as 155:2\'s rebel. Fresh.')
